[00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.560]   Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for standing by and welcome to the Ingersoll Rand First Quarter 2020 Earnings Conference Call.
[00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.080]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.920]   After the speaker's presentation, there will be a question and answer session.
[00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.900]   To ask a question during the session, you will need to press star 1 on your telephone.
[00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.540]   We ask that you please limit yourself to one question and one follow-up.
[00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:30.020]   If you require any further assistance, please press star 0.
[00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.660]   I would now like to hand the conference over to your speaker today, Vic Kinney, Head of Investor Relations.
[00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.920]   Thank you. Please go ahead.
[00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.880]   Thank you and welcome to the Ingersoll Rand 2020 First Quarter Earnings Call.
[00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:51.340]   I'm Vic Kinney, Ingersoll Rand Investor Relations Leader, and with me today are Vicente Reynal, Chief Executive Officer, and Emily Weaver, Chief Financial Officer.
[00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:55.460]   Our earnings release, which was issued this morning, and a supplemental presentation,
[00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:02.480]   which will be referenced during the call, are both available on the Investor Relations section of our website, www.irco.com.
[00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.280]   In addition, a replay of this morning's conference call will be available later today.
[00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:12.160]   Before we get started, I would like to remind everyone that certain of the statements on this call are forward-looking in nature
[00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.020]   and are subject to the risks and uncertainties discussed in our previous SEC filings,
[00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.820]   which you should read in conjunction with the information provided on this call.
